0. Additional Use Grant

    "You" means the natural person or Legal Entity exercising the rights in
    this License. All operation of the Licensed Work by any automated agent,
    bot, script, or AI system is attributed to the natural person or Legal
    Entity that controls, configures, directs, or benefits from that agent
    (the "Principal"). An agent is never the user.

    (a) Individuals. If you are a natural person acting on your own account
        (see 0(g)), you may use the Licensed Work free of charge for:

        (1) personal security research and education, subject to 0(e);

        (2) participation in bug bounty programs, vulnerability disclosure
            programs, and capture-the-flag exercises — including
            professional participation for which you receive monetary
            rewards. "Bug bounty program" means a program published by the
            target organization or hosted on an established
            vulnerability-reward platform, under terms offered uniformly to
            all participants or invited participants, that rewards accepted
            vulnerability reports. It does not include any arrangement under
            which you are contractually obligated to deliver testing
            services or findings to a specific client for agreed
            compensation;

        (3) automation of your own non-commercial workflows on systems you
            own or are authorized to test under 0(f) — this bullet does not
            extend to paid engagements for or on behalf of any client or
            employer.

        For the avoidance of doubt and notwithstanding anything to the
        contrary: a single natural person may run any number of automated
        agents, on any number of machines, around the clock, and may earn
        unlimited income from participation in bug bounty programs as
        defined in 0(a)(2), all free of charge — provided every operation of
        the Licensed Work is performed or personally directed by that
        person, all findings are submitted under that person's own identity
        and accounts, and no other person operates, supervises, or maintains
        the Licensed Work for that person's benefit.

    (b) Legal entities. If you are a Legal Entity (see 0(k)), you may use the
        Licensed Work free of charge only for:

        (1) internal security research, meaning security research conducted
            by the entity's own personnel, solely for the entity's own
            defensive purposes, for the benefit of no third party, on
            systems the entity owns or is authorized to test under 0(f).
            Results may not be sold, licensed, repackaged, or incorporated
            into any commercial product or service; "internal" does not
            extend across separate Legal Entities, including Affiliates;

        (2) coordinated vulnerability disclosure to third parties regarding
            vulnerabilities the entity discovers, and authorized testing of
            systems the entity owns or is authorized to test under 0(f),
            provided that (i) the entity does not resell or productize the
            Licensed Work or the testing, and (ii) no compensation the
            entity receives is contingent on discovered vulnerabilities. A
            Legal Entity's participation in bug bounty programs for reward,
            and any client-directed testing, requires a paid license.

    (c) Commercial use — meaning any use not permitted by Section 0(a) or
        0(b) as qualified by this Section 0 — requires a paid license from
        the Licensor. The activities below are ILLUSTRATIVE, NOT EXHAUSTIVE.
        Commercial use includes, without limitation:

        (1) embedding, bundling, linking, or orchestrating the Licensed Work
