2. Limitations

The Licensor reserves all rights not expressly granted to you in this license.

"Use" means any exercise of the rights granted above, including executing,
running, installing, loading, configuring, invoking, making available, and
distributing the Licensed Work. Use by an automated agent or program is Use
by the Principal defined in Section 0.

The activities listed in Section 0(c) are illustrative, not exhaustive.
Commercial use means any use not permitted by Section 0(a) or Section 0(b) as
qualified by Section 0. For the avoidance of doubt: (i) bounty, reward, or
prize payments received by a natural person for activities within Section
0(a) are not commercial use; (ii) any use of the Licensed Work for the
benefit of, on behalf of, or within the scope of a client, customer, or
employer engagement is commercial use, except participation in bug bounty,
vulnerability disclosure, and CTF activities described in Section 0(a)(2);
and (iii) a Legal Entity that directs, provisions, orchestrates, or derives
revenue from the use of the Licensed Work by other persons is making
commercial use, whether or not it executes the Licensed Work itself.

